course: dictionary
lesson: 5068
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word instant can mean several things, so context tells you which one to use. «Send me an instant reply» means the reply comes straight away, with no waiting.
explain: «Instant noodles» are made very quickly, usually with hot water. Try swapping in quick: «quick noodles» still makes sense, so instant means quick to make here.
explain: As a noun, an instant is a very short moment. «For an instant, nobody moved» means for a tiny moment. Check by swapping in moment: «For a moment, nobody moved» fits, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Instant can be an adjective, as in «an instant reply», or a noun, as in «for an instant».
fact: «In an instant» means very quickly, in a very short time: «the squashed air rushes out all at once».
fact: «The instant (that)» means as soon as: «Call me the instant you arrive».
fact: «Instantly» is the adverb form, meaning straight away.
fact: Everyday examples include instant coffee, instant messaging and instant replay.
exercise: «Call me the instant you arrive.» What does instant mean here? | Very slowly | *As soon as | Before you have left home | Once a year
exercise: «A balloon bursts at a pin's touch because the stretched rubber rips apart in an instant.» What does in an instant mean? | Very loudly | Only sometimes | *Very quickly, in a very short time | After a long wait
exercise: «For an instant, nobody moved.» What is an instant in this sentence? | A long journey | A kind of food | *A very short moment | A loud noise
test: «Instant noodles» are ready quickly. What does instant mean in this phrase? | Very old | Full of salt | *Made very quickly, usually with hot water | Sitting still
test: «The instant (that) the bell rang, the children ran.» What does the instant (that) mean? | After lunch | *As soon as | Exactly one hour before | Never
exam: Which sentence uses instant as a noun? | «Instant noodles are quick.» | «An instant reply came back.» | *«For an instant, nobody moved.» | «She was instantly happy.»
